abstract: "A computable biophysical framework for the limits of reversible preservation: 251 audited nodes, 91 primary sources and 5 hash-locked preregistrations. Key result: a human brain requires a critical cooling rate of at most 0.425 C/min, 4.25 times more permissive than M22."
